# Who must review a change before it reaches main.
#
# Merging to main is what triggers a production apply (see
# .github/workflows/cloudflare.yml), so this file is part of the change
# control for live DNS and WAF -- not just a notification convenience.
#
# This file on its own only *requests* reviewers. To make it binding, turn on
# the following for `main` in Settings > Branches > branch protection:
#
#   * Require a pull request before merging
#   * Require review from Code Owners
#   * Do not allow bypassing the above settings
#
# Scheduled deviation detection commits to main directly and therefore has to
# be allowed to bypass branch protection -- see docs/14-deviation-detection.md
# for which actor to grant that to and why.

# Everything, unless a more specific rule below overrides it.
*                           @rostam-sodagari

# The parts that decide what reaches Cloudflare at all: the CI pipeline, the
# CLI that plans and applies, the validator and policy gate, and the Terraform
# modules. A change here affects every domain at once.
/.github/                   @rostam-sodagari
/cf.py                      @rostam-sodagari
/policy.yaml                @rostam-sodagari
/scripts/                   @rostam-sodagari
/modules/                   @rostam-sodagari

# Provider pinning: these lock files are what stop a plan silently picking up
# a new Cloudflare provider build.
**/.terraform.lock.hcl      @rostam-sodagari
